From 47d2ea009401de1eee17e738c7dda6bf63cec570 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:07:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Move startup context initialization from Bash into Rust

Rust now reads the external manual.md at runtime and puts it on the
clipboard in Command::Start (after create_rcfile, before pty::run), so
startup no longer runs `cvb manual.md` through Bash and leaves no
history entry. The wrapper keeps all history/state/cleanup logic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016BRop2mLESfcXeppM2JEsn
